Build against Proxmox's crates from their git repositories. Debian builds
pve-rs with the Proxmox crates packaged as Debian source packages
(librust-*-dev, in the local registry .cargo/config.toml points at); they are
not on crates.io. This drops that source replacement and adds a
[patch.crates-io] section pointing every Proxmox crate at its repository on
git.proxmox.com, at the commits current when pve-rs 0.16.1 was released
(2026-11-11): proxmox.git 9bf4383b6ad4, proxmox-ve-rs.git 7a086eb1259f
("ve-config: bump version to 0.12.0"), perlmod.git 16e273973b2d ("perlmod:
bump to 0.14.3"). files/Cargo.lock pins the whole graph.
Only the crates the build uses are patched (and files/Cargo.lock has no
[[patch.unused]] entries): the build is offline against vendored crates, and a
[patch] entry whose crate is not vendored fails with "patch location ... does
not contain packages matching ...".
The approach follows proxmox-nixos (pkgs/pve-rs, which patches crates-io with
local copies of the same repositories); written for FenrirOS.

--- a/pve-rs/.cargo/config.toml
+++ b/pve-rs/.cargo/config.toml
@@ -1,8 +1,2 @@
-[source]
-[source.debian-packages]
-directory = "/usr/share/cargo/registry"
-[source.crates-io]
-replace-with = "debian-packages"
-
 [profile.release]
 debug = true
--- a/pve-rs/Cargo.toml
+++ b/pve-rs/Cargo.toml
@@ -109,3 +109,44 @@
 # proxmox-time = { path = "../../proxmox/proxmox-time" }
 # proxmox-uuid = { path = "../../proxmox/proxmox-uuid" }
 # proxmox-worker-task = { path = "../../proxmox/proxmox-worker-task" }
